    "A": "Ordinary STANDARD fixture: no repository journal or execution fingerprint routing; reread task authority, actual HEAD/staged diff/notes and PLAN text; bounded reads/verification and ownership confirmation before further writes on restart.",
    "B": "Fixture-only current strict schema-2 protocol with unchanged fingerprints and actual PLAN receipt.",
    "C": "One hypothetical checkpoint variant binding HEAD, allowed content, PLAN, state and external-risk flag; deliberately omits protected/index fingerprints."
  },
  "oracleRules": [
    "HEAD, PLAN-index, protected-state drift, unknown external result, or unknown ownership require BLOCKED before automatic mutation/finalize.",
    "An authorized coherent batch without those conflicts is safe under the bounded task oracle.",
    "Dirty Allowed Paths still require BLOCKED at a separate strict prepare; task-oracle falseBlocked labels cost, not a protocol violation."
  ],
  "costDefinition": "Counter scope: fixture persistence after identical seed creation; one fileWrites per logical output write (atomic temporary write included once), actual File.Replace count, verification command invocations, explicit action derivation invocations, receipt writes, cleanup deletion and external retry dispatch. Seeding including experiment authority input, drift/authority injection, imported M1 setup, Git read commands and hashing excluded. No model/token/latency measurements.",
  "limitations": [
    "Deterministic cut points, not real process kills, power loss, fsync guarantees or Codex compliance.",
    "A/C are explicit fixture strategies, not shipped runtimes. A reads experiment-supplied task HEAD, original notes/PLAN text and risk/ownership input outside the repository; ordinary STANDARD does not necessarily provide those facts. A performs no execution fingerprint routing; hashes are separately collected by the oracle/reporter. Authority provenance/capture cost is excluded; this is not a generic restart classifier.",
    "ASCII paths and one app file only; same Git content seeds, commit identities may differ across fresh repositories.",
    "C only tests this one incomplete variant; findings do not disprove all lightweight designs.",
    "The unknown-ownership case also injects protected notes drift. B BLOCKED does not prove author identity binding or detection of concurrent ownership inside Allowed Paths; C unsafe progression in this case is not an independent ownership-only result.",
    "HumanInterventionRequired is a derived requirement, not observed human corrections. VERIFY_THEN_CONFIRM is read-only; unsafeContinuation labels automatic progression permission, not an actual conflicting write.",
    "No external request dispatched; unknown external risk tests zero retry only.",
    "Scope counters do not measure real workflow cost or comparative performance."
  ],
